      "text": [
        " اَلسَّفَرِ ثُمَّ يَبْدُو لَهُ فِي اَلْإِقَامَةِ وَ هُوَ فِي اَلصَّلاَةِ قَالَ «يُتِمُّ إِذَا بَدَتْ لَهُ اَلْإِقَامَةُ»\nوَ عَنِ اَلرَّجُلِ يُشَيِّعُ أَخَاهُ إِلَى اَلْمَكَانِ اَلَّذِي يَجِبُ عَلَيْهِ فِيهِ اَلتَّقْصِيرُ وَ اَلْإِفْطَارُ قَالَ «لاَ بَأْسَ بِذَلِكَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1298 - Ali ibn Yaqtin asked Abu al-Hasan (as) about a man who sets out on a journey and then decides to stay (reside) while he is in the midst of prayer.\nImam (as) said: \"He should complete (the full prayer) when he decides to stay.\"\nHe also asked about a man who accompanies his brother to the point where shortening prayers and breaking the fast becomes obligatory.\nImam (as) said: \"There is no harm in that.\""
        ]
      }
